%% Logistics OS - Order-to-Cash event flow (choreography)
%% Rendering: Mermaid sequenceDiagram. See docs/events.md for topics.
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant CH as Channel/EDI
  participant OMS as OMS
  participant ORCH as Orchestrator
  participant ATP as ATP/Promise
  participant INTEL as Intelligence
  participant INV as Inventory view
  participant TMS as TMS
  participant WMS as WMS
  participant YMS as YMS
  participant VIS as Visibility
  participant FIN as Billing
  participant BUS as Kafka Backbone

  CH->>OMS: SubmitOrder
  OMS->>BUS: ord.order.created.v1
  BUS->>ORCH: order.created
  ORCH->>ATP: ReserveAtp(order)
  ATP->>INV: query availability
  ATP->>INTEL: GetEta / GetPlacement
  ATP-->>ORCH: Promise(date, node)
  ORCH->>BUS: orch.promise.v1
  ORCH->>OMS: ConfirmOrder
  OMS->>BUS: ord.order.confirmed.v1
  ORCH->>WMS: Allocate/Pick command
  WMS->>BUS: wms.task.events.v1
  ORCH->>TMS: TenderShipment command
  TMS->>BUS: tms.tender.events.v1
  TMS->>BUS: tms.shipment.events.v1
  BUS->>YMS: shipment.departed (schedule dock)
  YMS->>BUS: yms.yard.events.v1
  VIS->>BUS: vis.milestone.events.v1
  TMS->>BUS: tms.shipment.delivered
  BUS->>FIN: shipment.delivered (accrue/charge)
  FIN->>BUS: fin.settlement.events.v1
  Note over ORCH: Exceptions always emitted on orch.exception.v1
